WEBVTT

00:01.380 --> 00:05.829
Falco. Where are you
headed this late?

00:05.913 --> 00:07.429
Left something at HQ,

00:07.513 --> 00:10.429
so I'm running back there
to grab it real quick.

00:10.513 --> 00:11.644
See you later!

00:17.646 --> 00:20.696
Falco, could you do me a favor?

00:20.780 --> 00:22.744
Sure. What do you need?

00:23.713 --> 00:26.429
I want to send a letter, but

00:26.513 --> 00:28.429
coming from the internment zone,

00:28.513 --> 00:30.029
it'll probably be checked, right?

00:30.113 --> 00:31.629
Yeah, probably.

00:31.713 --> 00:32.829
If they see what I wrote,

00:32.913 --> 00:34.763
they'll know I shouldn't be here.

00:34.847 --> 00:35.897
Would you be willing to send it

00:35.981 --> 00:37.829
from outside the internment zone?

00:37.913 --> 00:41.629
Sure thing. Guess this
is to your family?

00:41.713 --> 00:44.563
Yeah. Just letting
them know that I'm here

00:44.647 --> 00:46.577
and that I'm all right.

02:31.087 --> 02:34.669
Hm? Hey. Why all the commotion?

02:34.753 --> 02:36.269
The Tybur family just arrived.

02:36.353 --> 02:37.669
Looks like all of them.

02:37.753 --> 02:39.517
Excuse me?

02:43.686 --> 02:45.269
They're the Tyburs' personal guard.

02:45.352 --> 02:46.936
It's an independent force.

02:47.020 --> 02:48.019
I hear they're good.

02:49.287 --> 02:50.669
Please come in.

02:50.753 --> 02:53.084
Sorry to drop in unannounced.

02:54.221 --> 02:57.803
I'm Willy. Head of
the Tyburs. It's a pleasure.

02:57.887 --> 03:01.003
I lead Marley's Warrior Unit.
Commander Theo Magath.

03:01.087 --> 03:04.602
It is an honor to make your
acquaintance, Lord Tybur.

03:04.686 --> 03:06.869
The feeling's mutual, Commander Magath.

03:06.953 --> 03:10.069
Now then. Allow me to introduce
you to my beloved family.

03:10.153 --> 03:12.069
I told you to stay still!

03:12.153 --> 03:13.683
Let him go!

03:15.753 --> 03:17.869
Now look what you've done!

03:17.953 --> 03:20.269
You've overseen the
Warrior unit quite successfully,

03:20.352 --> 03:22.736
Commander, so I'm curious.

03:22.820 --> 03:25.869
Can you tell which of us
is the War Hammer Titan?

03:25.953 --> 03:28.669
No, sir. I've seen
no sign at all.

03:28.753 --> 03:29.803
Frankly, I'm not even sure if

03:29.887 --> 03:31.736
the War Hammer came here with you.

03:31.820 --> 03:36.602
You have an
astute mind. As I'd heard.

03:36.686 --> 03:38.936
But no. It is here.

03:39.020 --> 03:42.450
Someone among us wields the War Hammer.

03:48.286 --> 03:52.269
I came here to lay eyes
on the statue of Helos.

03:52.352 --> 03:54.669
It captures the moment, a century ago,

03:54.753 --> 03:58.270
when a mere human struck down
the Devil of All Earth,

03:58.353 --> 04:01.018
saving the world and becoming a hero.

04:02.221 --> 04:04.069
What a grand sight.

04:04.153 --> 04:07.803
He stands brave and beautiful.
Not a scratch on him.

04:07.887 --> 04:11.003
Truly. This is
the spirit of Marley.

04:11.087 --> 04:12.869
Yes, I agree with you.

04:12.953 --> 04:15.203
Especially since the
statue's completely hollow.

04:15.286 --> 04:19.937
You're an unsparing critic, Commander.

04:20.021 --> 04:21.803
I'm told that you've been
working to reinstate

04:21.887 --> 04:24.203
conscription among Marleyan citizens.

04:24.286 --> 04:25.268
To the people of Marley,

04:25.352 --> 04:29.269
war exists only in the
pages of their newspapers.

04:29.353 --> 04:32.069
They read words saying
that the border's expanded,

04:32.153 --> 04:33.603
and they feel pride.

04:33.687 --> 04:35.003
If it's our tamed devils,

04:35.087 --> 04:37.003
or conscripts from conquered nations

04:37.087 --> 04:40.203
that bleed for those lands,
so much the better.

04:40.286 --> 04:43.203
I suppose the hope is that
by forcing Marleyan citizens

04:43.286 --> 04:45.269
to risk their own necks in the trenches,

04:45.353 --> 04:47.803
then we can eventually
put a halt to this nation's

04:47.887 --> 04:50.551
self-destructive march toward war.

04:53.887 --> 04:55.603
But if I had the ear of the man

04:55.687 --> 04:58.003
controlling Marley from the shadows,

04:58.087 --> 05:00.669
I would tell him it's too late.

05:00.753 --> 05:04.869
You truly don't hold back, do you?

05:04.953 --> 05:06.603
What am I to say?

05:06.687 --> 05:07.869
As you just noted,

05:07.953 --> 05:11.003
Marley is under the
Tybur family's influence.

05:11.087 --> 05:14.869
But we did not set Marley
on this path of militarism.

05:14.953 --> 05:17.202
The nation chose that for itself.

05:17.286 --> 05:19.937
Long ago, we Tyburs gave Marley freedom

05:20.021 --> 05:22.803
and power by way of atonement.

05:22.887 --> 05:25.137
We chose to stand by and watch

05:25.220 --> 05:28.217
as this country plunged
itself into darkness.

05:29.887 --> 05:32.202
We intend to reveal
everything to the world

05:32.286 --> 05:34.869
during the main event of the festival.

05:34.953 --> 05:38.603
When I said I'd come to see
the hero's statue, I meant it.

05:38.687 --> 05:40.851
Marley needs a new Helos.

05:42.087 --> 05:43.937
Theo Magath.

05:44.021 --> 05:47.151
I ask you to take my hand
and work at my side.

05:57.353 --> 05:58.937
Good morning, Pock!

05:59.021 --> 06:03.536
Hey, Pieck.
Why are you down there?

06:03.620 --> 06:06.069
I guess this just feels
more natural to me.

06:06.152 --> 06:08.050
Sorry if I scared you.

06:08.753 --> 06:11.617
Would'ja please just walk normal?

06:12.220 --> 06:14.003
Most Titans come from the south,

06:14.087 --> 06:17.069
so Paradis' defenses are heaviest there,

06:17.152 --> 06:19.803
and comparatively sparse
towards the northern mountains.

06:19.887 --> 06:22.269
I see. So we should
attack from the north.

06:22.353 --> 06:24.536
It's worth considering at least.

06:24.620 --> 06:27.869
However, we need to land a great
many troops and supplies,

06:27.953 --> 06:30.003
and for our largest ships to dock,

06:30.087 --> 06:32.069
we'll need control of
that southern wharf.

06:32.152 --> 06:34.069
Then we should come from the south.

06:34.152 --> 06:35.803
Not necessarily.

06:35.887 --> 06:37.269
We'd be sailing straight to the spot

06:37.353 --> 06:39.069
where we lost our scout ships.

06:39.152 --> 06:40.803
Its where the enemy's focused.

06:40.887 --> 06:42.669
They might've even torn the wharf down.

06:42.753 --> 06:45.269
All right. Then what are
you trying to say?

06:45.353 --> 06:47.269
I was just sharing
information that I thought

06:47.353 --> 06:49.069
you might find useful, sir.

06:49.152 --> 06:51.202
Well, I think you've shared quite enough.

06:51.286 --> 06:54.584
I don't know why we let an
Eldian talk in the first place.

06:59.152 --> 07:02.069
The Paradis plan
seems to be coming right along.

07:02.152 --> 07:06.069
The brass in charge is oh so intelligent.

07:06.152 --> 07:08.803
I sure am excited to hear
what they come up with.

07:08.887 --> 07:10.536
Like entrusting the whole operation

07:10.620 --> 07:12.717
to four children with no support?

07:15.353 --> 07:16.517
Hm?

07:20.887 --> 07:24.451
He's winning.
Falco just passed Gabi.

07:28.021 --> 07:31.603
Heh. Look how they
celebrate that one win.

07:31.687 --> 07:34.869
Dumb kids. Ignorance
really is bliss.

07:34.953 --> 07:36.869
But it doesn't matter how well Falco does

07:36.953 --> 07:38.269
from this point, does it?

07:38.353 --> 07:40.750
I mean Gabi's so far ahead of him.

07:41.487 --> 07:44.003
Did you see how he
took off at the last stretch?

07:44.086 --> 07:46.803
Hey there, kids.
What's all the fuss about?

07:46.887 --> 07:49.269
Falco finally got the best of Gabi!

07:49.353 --> 07:51.603
Really? He beat her grades?

07:51.687 --> 07:53.669
No. He just
outran her in a race.

07:53.753 --> 07:56.068
Sure, but it's still a historic feat!

07:56.152 --> 07:59.536
Hey. Can you cut it out?
Seriously, it's embarrassing.

07:59.620 --> 08:01.068
Pretty impressive!

08:01.152 --> 08:03.884
It sounds like maybe you're
gonna be the next Armor!

08:05.753 --> 08:07.669
There's no point in
trying to beat me now,

08:07.753 --> 08:09.003
it's too little too late!

08:09.086 --> 08:11.003
In case you forgot, I heroically defended

08:11.086 --> 08:12.984
our motherland in battle!

08:13.953 --> 08:17.669
Yeah, I know, but there's still a chance.

08:17.753 --> 08:20.269
They haven't announced
a successor quite yet,

08:20.353 --> 08:23.984
and until they do,
I'll keep on working my hardest.

08:25.953 --> 08:29.603
All right. Said like
a professional Warrior.

08:29.687 --> 08:31.068
Your brother's inheriting the Beast,

08:31.152 --> 08:32.202
so you and your family'll be made

08:32.286 --> 08:34.803
Honorary Marleyans no matter what you do!

08:34.887 --> 08:37.718
You know that, so why try so hard?

08:42.620 --> 08:44.869
I'm doing this for you!

08:44.953 --> 08:46.069
Falco...

08:46.153 --> 08:48.184
He really just up and said it!

08:51.753 --> 08:54.937
Huh?! You're trying to stop me
from getting what I want

08:55.020 --> 08:57.069
but you think you're doing it for me?

08:57.153 --> 08:59.869
That doesn't make any damn sense!

08:59.953 --> 09:02.269
He couldn't get through to her.

09:02.353 --> 09:04.869
Huh? What's that jerk's problem?

09:04.953 --> 09:07.136
Hey! Tell me!

09:07.220 --> 09:08.737
Well if it isn't our brave young

09:08.821 --> 09:10.869
Warriors-in-training.

09:10.953 --> 09:14.136
Gabi!
I heard what you did, Gabi!

09:14.220 --> 09:17.136
You're a hero to all
us Eldians, you know that?

09:17.220 --> 09:18.937
Thanks for your service!

09:19.020 --> 09:21.136
Sorry, but I'm just Zofia.

09:21.220 --> 09:22.669
Huh?

09:22.753 --> 09:23.869
Stop that, you stupid lush!

09:23.952 --> 09:26.202
Between the day-drinking and
the grabbing onto random girls,

09:26.286 --> 09:28.269
I've had it up to here with you!

09:28.353 --> 09:30.603
Shut up, you nosy old bat!

09:30.687 --> 09:32.669
Ain't nothing wrong with
givin' a hero due praise!

09:32.753 --> 09:33.869
There wouldn't be, except getting praised

09:33.952 --> 09:36.002
by someone like you is bad luck!

09:36.086 --> 09:39.017
Now go! Drag yourself home
to your poor mother!

09:40.887 --> 09:44.002
Now. Allow me to give
you kids a nice treat.

09:44.086 --> 09:45.203
Eat up, okay?

09:45.287 --> 09:48.803
I want you to get big and
strong like Vice Chief Braun!

09:48.887 --> 09:50.484
Thank you so much!

09:53.753 --> 09:57.269
Whoa. Are they
really gonna declare war

09:57.353 --> 09:59.669
from here in the internment zone?

09:59.753 --> 10:01.818
Looks like they're building a stage.

10:02.621 --> 10:04.203
They say leaders are gonna come from

10:04.287 --> 10:08.002
all over the world, and by
the time this festival is over,

10:08.086 --> 10:10.936
they're all gonna be on our side.

10:11.020 --> 10:12.284
Fantastic!

10:13.286 --> 10:14.803
Sounds like all of Marley's problems

10:14.887 --> 10:17.002
are about to magically disappear!

10:17.086 --> 10:19.203
You really don't think it'll work?

10:19.287 --> 10:21.136
Do you really think it will?

10:21.220 --> 10:23.737
We've been at war with
too many of these countries.

10:23.821 --> 10:26.002
They want Marley to fall.

10:26.086 --> 10:27.803
We aren't treated well here,

10:27.886 --> 10:30.669
but compared to the hatred
that Eldians face abroad,

10:30.753 --> 10:32.217
we're actually lucky.

10:32.886 --> 10:35.737
My family came from
a foreign internment zone.

10:35.821 --> 10:37.002
It was awful.

10:37.086 --> 10:41.002
Well. That's all the more reason
why we have to do something.

10:41.086 --> 10:43.269
They chose to meet
at the internment zone.

10:43.353 --> 10:45.803
Maybe they wanna help
people understand us.

10:45.886 --> 10:48.803
This is our chance to show the
world that we aren't devils.

10:48.886 --> 10:50.002
Okay, but how?

10:50.086 --> 10:53.202
Smile! I know how
badly you wanna be right,

10:53.286 --> 10:55.202
but right now, you can't be.

10:55.286 --> 10:57.603
Help prove yourself wrong
or we're all screwed.

10:57.687 --> 10:58.868
You shape up, too.

10:58.952 --> 11:01.002
Stop pretending to be a weirdo, Zofia.

11:01.086 --> 11:03.669
Um. This is just who I am.

11:03.753 --> 11:06.737
Fine. So what
are you gonna fix?

11:06.821 --> 11:11.002
Huh? There's nothing for
me to fix, I'm perfect.

11:11.086 --> 11:13.203
I'm sharp as a needle
and cute as a button.

11:13.287 --> 11:15.868
And when I captivate all the VIPs,

11:15.952 --> 11:18.803
my spot's gonna be that much more secure.

11:18.886 --> 11:21.203
Are you sure you're not a devil?

11:21.287 --> 11:24.537
And if you two ever cheer
for Falco over me again,

11:24.621 --> 11:25.603
I will make you cry.

11:25.687 --> 11:28.002
Oh, she's definitely a devil.

11:28.086 --> 11:31.737
It's Commander Magath.

11:31.820 --> 11:32.884
Here.

11:37.153 --> 11:39.669
Hmm. Is such a large-scale

11:39.753 --> 11:41.803
demolition necessary?

11:41.886 --> 11:44.817
Much of the structure has
decayed beyond repair.

11:48.287 --> 11:50.203
Allow me to congratulate you.

11:50.287 --> 11:52.603
The army is now yours, General.

11:52.687 --> 11:55.669
No, sir. It belongs
to the nation.

11:55.753 --> 11:57.869
And Marley is a nation commanded

11:57.953 --> 12:00.002
by none other than you, Lord Tybur.

12:00.086 --> 12:03.269
Hm. This nation
isn't mine, though.

12:03.353 --> 12:06.203
It belongs to the people:
Marleyan and Eldian.

12:06.287 --> 12:08.002
Now that I have the wheel,

12:08.086 --> 12:11.669
I can see why no one's
tried to turn it before.

12:11.753 --> 12:13.151
It's too heavy.

12:14.753 --> 12:16.802
I want nothing more than to let it go,

12:16.886 --> 12:20.050
but the time has come when I must not.

12:21.687 --> 12:23.869
It just happened to be me.

12:23.953 --> 12:28.603
By sheer chance, I happened to
be the man that fate turned to.

12:28.687 --> 12:30.869
The house was on the verge of collapse,

12:30.953 --> 12:34.269
but a few of its pillars remain usable.

12:34.353 --> 12:39.117
And according to them, the house
is already infested with rats.

12:41.621 --> 12:43.203
Nicely done, Falco.

12:43.287 --> 12:45.936
It's thanks to what
you said, Mr. Kruger!

12:46.020 --> 12:48.203
Honestly, I doubt I'll catch up to Gabi,

12:48.287 --> 12:50.869
no matter how hard I push myself.

12:50.953 --> 12:54.069
But even so, I'm gonna
keep moving forward.

12:54.153 --> 12:56.203
I see.

12:56.287 --> 12:59.269
I would still say that
I'm in your debt though.

12:59.353 --> 13:03.269
Thank you for delivering
those letters for me.

13:03.353 --> 13:04.802
You've been a big help.

13:04.886 --> 13:07.117
Huh? Oh, sure.

13:08.820 --> 13:12.002
That glove. Did your
family send it to you?

13:12.086 --> 13:15.802
They thought it would make
hospital life less boring.

13:15.886 --> 13:19.203
It's hard to do much in this shape, but

13:19.287 --> 13:21.936
I need to move forward, too.

13:22.020 --> 13:25.784
After the festival,
I'm going back to my hometown.

13:27.087 --> 13:29.269
Glad to hear it.

13:29.353 --> 13:32.003
A doctor's coming.

13:32.087 --> 13:33.869
Well. I should head out.

13:33.953 --> 13:34.950
Yeah.

13:37.220 --> 13:39.802
Would you mind if I sit next to you?

13:39.886 --> 13:41.618
Sure. Why not?

13:42.487 --> 13:44.817
Thanks, I appreciate it.

13:47.287 --> 13:50.136
My name's Jaeger. I'm an
Internment Zone physician.

13:50.220 --> 13:54.003
I like to come out here and
drink tea from time to time.

13:54.087 --> 13:57.670
Good to meet you. I'm Kruger.

13:57.753 --> 13:59.269
Good to meet you, too.

13:59.353 --> 14:03.603
I saw you speaking with a boy
just now. Is he a friend?

14:03.686 --> 14:04.869
Guess so.

14:04.953 --> 14:08.802
Hmm. I wonder
if he could've been my friend.

14:08.886 --> 14:12.817
After all, I too sit here,
looking for someone to talk to.

14:13.886 --> 14:16.269
Before the Eldian
Restorationists were caught,

14:16.353 --> 14:19.069
that boy's uncle was a leading member.

14:19.153 --> 14:21.069
Marley sends captured restorationists

14:21.153 --> 14:22.002
straight to paradise,

14:22.086 --> 14:24.869
frequently with their family's in tow.

14:24.953 --> 14:26.669
In order to protect their loved ones,

14:26.753 --> 14:30.002
the boy and his brother said
they wanted to become Warriors.

14:30.086 --> 14:32.069
And now, his brother has been chosen

14:32.153 --> 14:34.069
to inherit the Beast Titan.

14:34.153 --> 14:38.084
Which means the Grice family
is finally safe again.

14:39.287 --> 14:43.003
Hold on. Why tell me all this?

14:43.087 --> 14:45.003
So that you'll stop asking that young man

14:45.087 --> 14:47.003
to run errands for you.

14:47.087 --> 14:49.736
The Grice family's efforts
will have been for nothing

14:49.820 --> 14:52.802
if people begin to suspect
him of something illicit.

14:52.886 --> 14:55.802
And if your heart and mind
truly are healthy,

14:55.886 --> 14:58.736
you should go back to your family now.

14:58.820 --> 15:01.203
The people you love
won't always be waiting.

15:01.287 --> 15:04.984
If you take them for granted,
you will be left with regret.

15:06.287 --> 15:08.717
Will I? I see.

15:12.087 --> 15:15.350
You have regrets about your own family?

15:17.753 --> 15:20.537
I'm filled with them. Even now.

15:20.620 --> 15:22.269
I was so hard on my son.

15:22.353 --> 15:25.069
So insistent that he become a doctor.

15:25.153 --> 15:28.537
That's why he took his sister
outside the walls.

15:28.620 --> 15:30.269
That's why she...

15:30.353 --> 15:31.403
She...

15:31.487 --> 15:36.550
It's
my fault. It's all my fault!

15:41.820 --> 15:43.269
Mr. Jaeger!

15:43.353 --> 15:45.802
Please don't go outside unsupervised!

15:45.886 --> 15:49.084
Sorry about this. I only
looked away for a moment.

15:50.087 --> 15:52.269
Come along, Mr. Jaeger.

15:52.353 --> 15:54.817
Everything will be all right.

16:13.785 --> 16:14.701
This is crazy.

16:14.785 --> 16:17.100
I've seen these people in the papers.

16:17.184 --> 16:19.167
Enough idle chitchat.

16:19.251 --> 16:21.767
We're gonna serve these people
so well that their heads spin.

16:21.851 --> 16:23.767
Look, they're starting
to leave dirty dishes.

16:23.851 --> 16:24.982
Get 'em!

16:28.184 --> 16:29.301
Yes.

16:29.385 --> 16:31.182
I've always felt that way.

16:33.518 --> 16:34.567
Falco, drink!

16:34.651 --> 16:35.483
Here!

16:37.651 --> 16:42.567
Huh? Look. They're letting some
filthy-blood carry our plates.

16:42.651 --> 16:46.549
Ugh. No wonder
the food here reeks.

16:50.518 --> 16:52.501
I-I'm terribly sorry, ma'am!

16:52.585 --> 16:54.767
Shh! Don't make a scene of it.

16:54.851 --> 16:57.634
But the wine.
It stained your outfit.

16:57.718 --> 17:01.167
My lady. Is everything
all right?

17:01.251 --> 17:04.434
This is quite embarrassing,
but I spilled wine on my kimono

17:04.518 --> 17:07.367
and was just asking
this boy for assistance.

17:07.451 --> 17:08.367
Thank you, young man.

17:08.451 --> 17:10.367
I'm so sorry to hear that.

17:10.451 --> 17:12.034
Please come right this way.

17:12.118 --> 17:14.167
Wh-Why would you...?

17:14.251 --> 17:15.701
There's no telling what
they would've done to you

17:15.785 --> 17:17.649
if I'd been honest, right?

17:18.719 --> 17:20.501
Are you okay?

17:20.585 --> 17:23.767
Yeah. She saved me.

17:23.851 --> 17:26.501
Even though she knew that I'm an Eldian.

17:26.585 --> 17:28.634
I think I know why.

17:28.718 --> 17:32.282
That woman's probably
an Easterner from Hizuru.

17:36.384 --> 17:38.082
It's Willy Tybur!

17:39.318 --> 17:40.701
Willy!

17:40.785 --> 17:43.167
If it isn't the heir of our saviors!

17:43.251 --> 17:46.367
Ambassador Ogweno!
Long time no see!

17:46.451 --> 17:49.567
And Nambia! It's been
since we were children.

17:49.651 --> 17:52.701
Yes. Sorry for
all the times I made you cry.

17:52.785 --> 17:55.034
I wonder if you remember this, Willy.

17:55.118 --> 17:58.315
Oh! Of course, from when
you fell out of that tree!

18:03.719 --> 18:06.034
Let me bid you a warm welcome

18:06.118 --> 18:09.434
and offer my thanks to
you all for traveling so far.

18:09.518 --> 18:12.367
Until very recently,
some of us were engaged

18:12.451 --> 18:16.301
in a rather unseemly
dispute over resources.

18:16.385 --> 18:19.948
However, yesterday's enemy
is today's enemy!

18:20.785 --> 18:21.767
Pardon.

18:21.851 --> 18:24.635
I mean yesterday's enemy
is today's friend!

18:24.719 --> 18:26.367
Let us wash the past down the toilet

18:26.451 --> 18:29.167
alongside our drinks tonight!

18:29.251 --> 18:30.767
Toward that end,
please raise your glasses

18:30.851 --> 18:32.701
and join me for a toast!

18:32.785 --> 18:35.716
Cheers! To everlasting peace!

18:37.651 --> 18:40.034
Such a refined joke!

18:40.118 --> 18:42.100
It's unfortunate that
this isn't a first language

18:42.184 --> 18:43.767
for all our guests.

18:43.851 --> 18:45.501
You weren't quite understood.

18:45.585 --> 18:47.701
So please, allow me
to take over from here.

18:47.785 --> 18:50.034
Thanks for breaking the ice, Ambassador.

18:50.118 --> 18:51.434
All right, Willy!

18:51.518 --> 18:53.515
Kin of our saviors!

18:57.318 --> 18:59.701
You've been invited to join me tomorrow,

18:59.785 --> 19:02.100
in the Liberio Internment Zone.

19:02.184 --> 19:06.181
It is home to a people whose
blood runs through my own veins.

19:07.118 --> 19:10.167
These people are known
to be descendants of devils,

19:10.251 --> 19:14.034
for their ancestors
massacred untold millions.

19:14.118 --> 19:17.301
And strangely, after enduring
the worst of their cruelty,

19:17.385 --> 19:20.367
Marley used those devils
to oppress other nations,

19:20.451 --> 19:23.234
repeating the horrors of the past.

19:23.318 --> 19:27.434
Would the world not be better
if Titans ceased to exist?

19:27.518 --> 19:30.767
There is but one answer
to the Eldian question.

19:30.850 --> 19:34.034
After years of searching, I've found it.

19:34.118 --> 19:36.100
And tomorrow night, I'll share it

19:36.184 --> 19:38.767
in the course of my first-ever
theatrical production.

19:38.850 --> 19:41.501
I hope that each of you will be there.

19:41.585 --> 19:45.367
Now. To the playwrights
and the witnesses of history!

19:45.451 --> 19:48.682
To the playwrights
and the witnesses of history!

20:02.850 --> 20:04.448
What the hell?

20:16.451 --> 20:18.167
What is all this?

20:18.251 --> 20:19.367
Gabi!

20:19.451 --> 20:20.367
About time you woke up!

20:20.451 --> 20:22.167
Why is everything all crazy?

20:22.251 --> 20:23.501
It's for the festival!

20:23.585 --> 20:24.701
Different people have been pouring in

20:24.784 --> 20:26.367
from outside all morning,

20:26.451 --> 20:28.101
and they opened up
a bunch of food stalls!

20:28.185 --> 20:29.615
Here, try this!

20:30.518 --> 20:32.567
It's the best thing I've ever tasted!

20:32.651 --> 20:34.149
Let's go!

21:01.385 --> 21:04.101
Ugh. It hurts!

21:04.185 --> 21:07.435
That's what you get for being a glutton.

21:07.519 --> 21:09.167
Look at the flags they put up!

21:09.251 --> 21:12.167
They should just
make every day a festival.

21:12.251 --> 21:13.367
Think so, huh?

21:13.451 --> 21:16.100
It probably  nothing, but I've
noticed a lot of new things

21:16.184 --> 21:18.367
have been happening in the last few days.

21:18.451 --> 21:20.234
Is that right?

21:20.318 --> 21:21.701
It feels strange.

21:21.784 --> 21:25.567
As if the world is about to
change in a big way.

21:25.651 --> 21:28.182
Yeah. I hear you.

22:33.846 --> 22:36.562
Hey. How've you
enjoyed the festival?

22:36.646 --> 22:38.695
Wait. Where's Falco?

22:38.779 --> 22:41.430
Oh. He said he saw someone
he knew in the crowd

22:41.514 --> 22:42.762
and ran off to say hi.

22:42.846 --> 22:45.496
Huh. Hope this doesn't
make him late.

22:45.580 --> 22:47.362
Man. You really can't loosen up

22:47.446 --> 22:49.162
without booze, can you?

22:49.246 --> 22:50.562
Look at all these people.

22:50.646 --> 22:52.762
Look there. I guess
he made it back.

22:52.846 --> 22:55.296
Mr. Braun!

22:55.380 --> 22:57.029
Where the hell have you been?

22:57.113 --> 22:59.562
Sir. Do you mind coming with me?

22:59.646 --> 23:00.762
Don't think there's time.

23:00.846 --> 23:02.362
Ah, you'll be fine.

23:02.446 --> 23:05.562
The curtains won't go up
for a few more minutes.

23:05.645 --> 23:07.296
Over this way!

23:07.380 --> 23:09.362
What's this about, Falco?

23:09.446 --> 23:11.477
You can see for yourself in a second.

23:15.645 --> 23:17.762
It's through this door!

23:17.846 --> 23:19.210
okay...

23:22.779 --> 23:24.477
I got him to come!

23:26.246 --> 23:31.977
Evening. It's been
four years... Reiner.

23:35.846 --> 23:37.144
Eren!

23:40.580 --> 23:44.496
Reiner faces Eren in
the gloom of a lamplit cellar.

23:44.580 --> 23:47.762
As Willy Tybur sweeps
his audience to their feet,

23:47.846 --> 23:49.362
Eren confesses.

23:49.446 --> 23:52.029
He and Reiner are the same.

23:52.113 --> 23:55.144
Next episode:
"Declaration of War."
